## PR composition

- Keep diffs small and focused.
- Title should describe the concrete change (what/where), not intent alone.
- Ensure all new links work and follow the docs style rules.

## Review checklist

- [ ] Correct folder and index updates (placement and navigation)
- [ ] Style conformance (headings, spacing, fences, newline at EOF)
- [ ] Relative links only; no bare URLs in prose
- [ ] Persona voice used only where appropriate
- [ ] Diagrams and examples render as expected

## Commits

- Prefer conventional, descriptive commit messages.
- If template automation exists, use the repository’s template flow (see `ai-template-rendering` rules).
